  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "A triangle of area $60\\text{ cm}^2$ has side lengths of $16\\text{ cm}$ and $20\\text{ cm}$. The angle included between these sides is acute. What is its magnitude, correct to the nearest degree?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$22^\\circ$",
      "worked": "Let $C$ be the included angle.\n$$\\begin{align*}60&=\\frac12(16)(20)\\sin C\\\\\\sin C&=\\frac{60}{160}\\\\\\sin C&=\\frac38\\\\C&=\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac38\\right)\\\\C&\\approx22^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\nThe included angle is acute, so the acute inverse-sine solution is required.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
